## 4. Conditions

### 4.1 No commercial use

You may not engage in Commercial Use of the Software or of any Derivative Work. Every copy and every Derivative Work that You distribute must be made available free of charge.

### 4.2 Credit is always required

Every copy and every Derivative Work, in source or compiled form, must:

1. keep this License and all copyright and attribution notices intact;
2. state clearly, in its documentation and in its “about” information or README, that it is based on Apsi, originally developed by **ATEC**, with the official source address **https://github.com/OWNER/apsi (to be published)**;
3. state that it was modified, if it was, and by whom.

The credit must be easy to find for an ordinary user. It may not be hidden, removed or made misleading.

### 4.3 The same license for derivative works

You must distribute Derivative Works only under this License, with its non-commercial and credit conditions unchanged. You may not add terms that restrict the rights this License gives to others.

### 4.4 No endorsement

The names “Apsi” and “ATEC” may be used to describe the origin of a Derivative Work as required by section 4.2, but not to suggest that ATEC endorses it. A modified version must not be presented as the official Apsi.

